  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Marathon Petroleum received $503M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Marathon Petroleum won 140 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $3.6M. Marathon Petroleum obligations are down 7.2% year over year. Marathon Petroleum has a multi-year presence in federal contracting, with reported obligations of $11.9M in FY21, $93.1M in FY22, $359M in FY23, $288M in FY24, $542M in FY25, and $503M in FY26. Marathon Petroleum shows a pronounced growth between FY21 and FY25, followed by a modest decline into FY26. Marathon Petroleum’s current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date obligations rather than full-year results. Marathon Petroleum’s award count and average award size indicate a mix of mid-sized contracts rather than a large number of very small awards. Marathon Petroleum’s year-over-year change offers a concise measure of current momentum in federal spending to the company during the ongoing fiscal year.",
